## The one PRODUCTION defect (log-sink `owningRoot`)
$ bun test packages/mpd-mcp-shared/log-sink.test.ts      # BEFORE
Expected: "C:\\Users\\ZHAO~1.YIN\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\mpd-log-sink-SQ7h8H"
Received: null
      at log-sink.test.ts:70:23          # the sink WROTE the file and still reported root: null
FIX: owningRoot now uses `relative(root, file)` + `isAbsolute` instead of a `${root}/` prefix with a
hard-coded forward slash.
$ bun test packages/mpd-mcp-shared/log-sink.test.ts      # AFTER
 9 pass / 0 fail

## The team-plane / QA `basename` defect
$ bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/team-plane.test.ts     # BEFORE
Expected: "/elsewhere/.mpd/boulder.json"
Received: "\\elsewhere\\.mpd\\boulder.json"
$ node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/session-start-team.ts --self-test   # BEFORE
  - c7: a record led by THIS session with 7 members must read leading, got {"leading":false,"members":0}
Both came from `path.slice(path.lastIndexOf("/") + 1)` (win32 paths carry `\`) and from POSIX path
literals where production uses `join`. FIX: `basename` + `join`-built expectations.
$ bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/team-plane.test.ts     # AFTER
 51 pass / 0 fail
$ node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/session-start-team.ts --self-test   # AFTER
 exit=0

## The QA `tui-deps-ctrla` sibling fixture
- a sibling install must fail the contact verdict            # BEFORE
FIX: `launched.replace("/profiles/dsh-tui", …)` matched nothing on win32 (join emits `\`), so the
'sibling' WAS the launched copy and the arm failed on a CORRECT verdict; the sibling is now built with
the separator the launched path itself uses.
$ bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/tui-deps-ctrla.ts --self-test    # AFTER
 exit=0

## The change-feed timing race (6 arms)
